/*  Operator overloads — `Pass2CheckOverloads`, `ResolveOperandType`, `CheckOperatorOverload` and
    `HasDirectFailureReturn` in `TypeChecker.Objects.cs`, and the lookup at the top of `InferBinary`.

    ★ In the tree: `(OperatorOverloadDeclaration <op> "lhs" "rhs" "left type" "right type" [body]
    line column)`. Keyed on the ORDERED pair of type names as written, so `vec2 * number` and
    `number * vec2` are two declarations, and a pair that is built-in arithmetic is refused.

    ★ Checked in a pass of their own, after the shared constants and before any statement, so a
    use above its declaration already knows what it gives back — read off the body's first
    `Return`, as a lambda's is. A body that can return a failure gives back `T or failure`.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind text to op-symbol, given (the text op):
        Judge op, where it is:
            "Plus", return "+".
            "Minus", return "-".
            "Star", return "*".
            "Slash", return "/".
            Otherwise, return op.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `OperandTypeName`: the name an operand is looked up under, or "" for a shape that has none.
    Bind text to operand-type-name, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType", return cast display-name on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1))).
        If shape's kind is "NumberType", return "number".
        If shape's kind is "TextType", return "text".
        If shape's kind is "FactType", return "fact".
        If shape's kind is "BitsType", return "bits".
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// `ResolveOperandType`: an object the program defined, or a built-in scalar.
    Bind node or failure to overload-operand unto checker, given (the text name, the number at-row):
        If cast one's definition-of on (name) is not void, return cast object-type-named on (name).
        Define lowered as name in lowercase.
        Judge lowered, where it is:
            "number", return cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
            "text", return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
            "fact", return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
            "bits", return cast plain-type on ("BitsType").
            Otherwise:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is not a defined object type — an operator overload has no type to register on", "",
                    at-row, "declare an overload for '{name}'",
                    "Define 'object {name}' before declaring operator overloads for it, or check the spelling.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `HasDirectFailureReturn`: a `return a failure` anywhere in the body but a nested one's.
    Bind fact to has-direct-failure-return, given (the node statements):
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "ReturnStatement":
                Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
                If cast is-nothing on (value) is false and cast is-failure-expression on (value), return true.
            Done.
            Define inner as a series of node.
            If kind is "WhileStatement" or kind is "PullStatement" or kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Insert cast field-of on (statement, 2) into inner.
            Done.
            If kind is "RepeatUntilStatement", insert cast field-of on (statement, 1) into inner.
            If kind is "ForEachStatement", insert cast field-of on (statement, 3) into inner.
            If kind is "WithOpenStatement", insert cast field-of on (statement, 4) into inner.
            If kind is "IfStatement":
                For each arm in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Insert cast field-of on (arm, 2) into inner.
                Done.
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) is false, insert cast field-of on (statement, 2) into inner.
            Done.
            If kind is "TryStatement":
                For each place in a series with (1, 2, 3), repeat:
                    If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, place)) is false, insert cast field-of on (statement, place) into inner.
                Done.
            Done.
            For each block in inner, repeat:
                If cast has-direct-failure-return on (block), return true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// `Pass2CheckOverloads`: every overload, refused or checked, in the order written.
    Bind void or failure to check-overloads unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (program), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration":
                Define op as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word.
                Define left-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
                Define right-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
                Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
                Define symbol as cast op-symbol on (op).
                Define left as cast one's overload-operand on (left-name, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                Define right as cast one's overload-operand on (right-name, at-row) or pass the failure off.
                If left's kind is right's kind and (left's kind is "NumberType" or left's kind is "BitsType"):
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{left-name} {symbol} {right-name}' already means something, so it cannot be overloaded",
                        "That is built-in arithmetic, and a built-in cannot be shadowed — otherwise '{symbol}' would mean one thing here and another everywhere else",
                        at-row, "overload '{symbol}' for '{left-name}' and '{right-name}'",
                        "Overload a pair that has no meaning yet — one with an object type in it, or something like 'text * number'.")).
                Done.
                Define key as "{left-name} {op} {right-name}".
                If (the entry for key in seen) is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{left-name} {symbol} {right-name}' already has an overload", "",
                        at-row, "declare a second '{symbol}' overload for that pair",
                        "Each operator can only be overloaded once per ORDERED pair of types. '{right-name} {symbol} {left-name}' is a different pair and may be declared separately.")).
                Done.
                In seen, the entry for key becomes true.
                Cast one's check-overload on (statement, left, right) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `CheckOperatorOverload`: the body sees what a top-level function sees, plus its two operands;
    /// what it gives back is read off its first `Return`.
    Bind void or failure to check-overload unto checker, given (the node statement, the node left, the node right):
        Define op as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word.
        Define left-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define right-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Define body as cast field-of on (statement, 6).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)).
        Define fallible as cast has-direct-failure-return on (body).

        Define saved as one's scopes.
        Define saved-types as the number of one's type-scopes.
        Define fresh as cast builtin-scope.
        Cast carry-modules on (saved, fresh).
        Define earlier-hidden as one's hidden.
        Define hiding as a map from text to fact.
        For each scope in saved, repeat:
            For each pair in scope, repeat:
                Define held as the value of pair.
                If held's shape's kind is "FunctionType" or held's permanent:
                    In fresh, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes held.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    In hiding, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        The one's hidden becomes hiding.
        The one's scopes becomes a series with (fresh).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        For each operand in a series with (2, 3), repeat:
            Define operand-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, operand)).
            Define operand-type as left.
            If operand is 3, the operand-type becomes right.
            Cast one's bind-name on (operand-name, a new binding {
                the shape operand-type, the established-by cast named-reference on (operand-name), the line at-row,
                the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
        Done.

        Define earlier-in-function as one's in-function.
        Define earlier-line as one's function-line.
        Define earlier-depth as one's rabbit-depth.
        Define earlier-inferring as one's inferring-lambda.
        Define earlier-fallible as one's overload-fallible.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes 0.
        Increment one's nesting by 1.
        The one's in-function becomes true.
        The one's inferring-lambda becomes true.
        The one's overload-fallible becomes fallible.
        Insert cast unknown-type into one's expected-returns.
        The one's function-line becomes at-row.

        Cast one's check-block on (body) or pass the failure off.
        If cast definitely-returns on (body) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the '{left-name} {cast op-symbol on (op)} {right-name}' overload can reach its end without returning a value", "",
                at-row, "define an operator overload that might not return a value",
                "Make sure every path through the overload ends with a return statement.")).
        Done.

        Define inferred as item (the number of one's expected-returns) of one's expected-returns.
        Remove item (the number of one's expected-returns) from one's expected-returns.
        The one's in-function becomes earlier-in-function.
        The one's inferring-lambda becomes earlier-inferring.
        The one's overload-fallible becomes earlier-fallible.
        The one's function-line becomes earlier-line.
        The one's rabbit-depth becomes earlier-depth.
        Decrement one's nesting by 1.
        The one's hidden becomes earlier-hidden.
        The one's scopes becomes saved.
        Cast one's trim-type-scopes on (saved-types).
        If cast is-none on (inferred) is false:
            In one's overloads, the entry for "{left-name} {op} {right-name}" becomes inferred.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The top of `InferBinary`: an operand pair with an overload takes it, ahead of anything else.
    /// Gives back what it gives, or `none` for a pair with no overload.
    Bind node or failure to overload-result unto checker, given (the text op, the node lhs, the node rhs, the number at-row):
        If op is not "Plus" and op is not "Minus" and op is not "Star" and op is not "Slash", return cast unknown-type.
        Define left-name as cast operand-type-name on (lhs).
        Define right-name as cast operand-type-name on (rhs).
        If left-name is "" or right-name is "", return cast unknown-type.
        Define found as the entry for "{left-name} {op} {right-name}" in one's overloads.
        If found is void, return cast unknown-type.
        If found's kind is "FailureType":
            Define symbol as cast op-symbol on (op).
            If one's in-try is false and one's handled is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{left-name} {symbol} {right-name}' can fail — you must handle the failure", "",
                    at-row, "use '{symbol}' on '{left-name}' and '{right-name}' without handling the potential failure",
                    "Wrap this in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block, or use 'but on failure <default>'.")).
            Done.
            If one's in-try, return cast field-of on (found, 1).
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.
Done.
